3. Internal deployment, browsers and service providers

You may make the copies needed to deploy the Software within Your
Organization, including delivery of JavaScript, CSS and related assets to
Authorized Users' browsers and devices. Private repositories, private
package registries, build systems and internal application deployments are
permitted. You must restrict access to Authorized Users and the service
providers described below, using reasonable access controls.

You may engage contractors and hosting, build, storage or other infrastructure
providers to develop, operate or maintain a permitted deployment solely on
Your Organization's behalf. You may supply them the copies needed for that
work, including on third-party cloud infrastructure. They must be bound by
contractual duties to limit use and access to that work, protect the copies,
and stop use and delete them when no longer needed, except legally required
or routine backup copies that remain protected and are not used otherwise.
You are responsible for their compliance when acting on Your behalf.

These limited copying and access permissions are exceptions to section 4;
they do not permit a provider to offer its own product or service containing
the Software to customers. Charging for contracted development or hosting
of Your permitted internal deployment is allowed. A provider may serve
multiple organizations only through separate deployments on behalf of each
organization exercising its own rights under this License; it may not use
this exception to offer a shared or white-label planner service.

4. No redistribution or external service

Except as expressly permitted by sections 3, 5, 6 and 8, You may not:

(a) distribute, publish, sell, rent, sublicense or otherwise supply the
    Software to anyone outside Your Organization, alone or incorporated in
    an application, library, template, container, SDK or other product;
(b) make the Software or its functionality available to customers or other
    external users, whether as SaaS (software as a service), a hosted or
    managed service, an API, a customer portal or another network service;
(c) use the Software to operate a service that processes third parties'
    planning requests on their behalf, even if they receive only outputs;
(d) enable another person to do any of the above on Your behalf.

These restrictions apply to original and modified versions, source and
compiled forms, free and paid offerings, and direct and indirect access.
An external user's own internal business purpose does not make a service
You provide to that user an internal deployment of Your Organization.
An externally hosted deployment used only as permitted by section 3 is
allowed; the location of a server does not determine whether use is internal.

